<h2>Asobi Review 1.0.22 (build 2357) <span class="when">Nov 25, 2026</span></h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Live links with a passphrase.</b> When a live link needs a passphrase, Asobi asks for it as the link opens. The words come from whoever sent the link.</li>
<li><b>Paste the whole invitation.</b> File &rsaquo; Open Live Link&hellip; now finds the live link inside whatever you paste, including a whole invitation from Asobi Live, and fills in just the link when one is on the clipboard.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<div class="earlier">Earlier updates</div>
<h3>1.0.21 (build 2340) <span class="when">Nov 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Live pictures.</b> A live link from a grading Mac opens in its own window: File &rsaquo; Open Live Link&hellip;, a link pasted into Join a Review, or Open in Asobi Review on the live page. The picture is shown through Asobi's color like a Rec.709 movie, with its sound. Quality follows your connection (Auto) or picks Full, HD or Low, and full screen fades the bar away while the mouse is still.</li>
<li><b>Display warnings.</b> When Night Shift or True Tone is changing the picture's color, an amber Display chip appears in the bar. It can turn them off while you review, and Asobi turns them back on when it quits. On an XDR display it suggests the HDTV Video (BT.709-BT.1886) preset for Rec.709 work. Settings &rsaquo; Interface &rsaquo; Display Warnings turns the chip off.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.20 (build 2325) <span class="when">Nov 24, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Kitsu comments in internal reviews.</b> When a review is marked Internal Review, everyone in it sees its Kitsu comments, including people on the web page. Client reviews still keep them on the host's Mac unless Show Kitsu Comments to Guests is on.</li>
<li><b>Joining a review in progress.</b> Someone who joins late now gets every comment on the right shot. A few could land on the shot they were leaving.</li>
<li><b>Next and previous comment across shots.</b> In a cut movie, Command-] past a shot's last comment goes on to the next shot that has one, and Command-[ goes back the same way.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.19 (build 2318) <span class="when">Nov 21, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Kitsu comments are in date order.</b> In This shot, a frame's notes from the review come first, in the order they were written, then its Kitsu comments, newest first.</li>
<li><b>Filter the notes.</b> The filter button beside Export shows four pop-ups: Who, When, Version and From (this review or Kitsu). The list says how many notes it is showing, and Clear brings them all back. It works in This shot, Whole movie and the Kitsu tab, stays on this Mac, and exports still take every note.</li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.18 (build 2315) <span class="when">Nov 21, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Behind-the-scenes fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.17 (build 2307) <span class="when">Nov 20, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Behind-the-scenes fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.16 (build 2304) <span class="when">Nov 20, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Behind-the-scenes fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
<h3>1.0.15 (build 2301) <span class="when">Nov 19, 2026</span></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Behind-the-scenes fixes.</b></li>
</ul>
]]></description>
